\frametitle{Filtering in code — the full toolbox}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python]
box    = cv2.blur(img, (5, 5))
gauss  = cv2.GaussianBlur(img, (7, 7), 1.5)
median = cv2.medianBlur(img, 3)             # nonlinear, impulse noise
bilat  = cv2.bilateralFilter(img, 9, 75, 75)# edge-preserving smooth
k = np.array([[0,-1,0],[-1,5,-1],[0,-1,0]])
sharp  = cv2.filter2D(img, -1, k)           # any custom kernel
\end{lstlisting}
  \code{cv2.filter2D} convolves with any kernel you give it — the general tool the others are shortcuts for.
